The first-parent main commit adding this marker prepares Runner persisted-v1
readers and bundled Guest consumers for bounded large decoded-storage inputs.
It retains the preceding small producer and outbound admission policy.

Once a later release enables larger positive v1 writes, supported Runner rollback
tags must descend from this reader-preparation commit. Stopping larger writers
does not remove their persisted entries. Resolve the merged main commit from
this marker rather than using a feature-branch SHA. Activation enforces this
floor; this preparation alone does not reject earlier rollback targets.
